Chapter: X509ChainTest
  cites Encode chapter X509Chain
  cites Encode chapter X509
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 The chain walk, on a chain made entirely of bytes the IETF published.

 RFC 8410 section 10.2's certificate is SELF-ISSUED -- its issuer and its
 subject are the same Name -- and it is signed by the Ed25519 key that RFC
 8410 section 10.1 publishes. So that key, under that name, is a genuine
 TRUST ANCHOR, and the certificate is a genuine one-link chain beneath it.
 Nothing here is minted by us and then graded by us.

 Every negative below is that same chain with exactly ONE thing changed,
 which is the only way to know that the rule you think you are testing is
 the rule that fired.

